-- A bare-value `main` whose value is a record FIELD ACCESS. Both halves are
-- load-bearing: `medaka build` and the WasmGC emitter wrap a bare-value `main` as
-- `main = println <e>` and re-run the check gate on the wrapped program BETWEEN the
-- two emit elaborations of `runEmitWith` (compiler/entries/entry_support.mdk), so a
-- ctor-oracle row that interleaved check leaves behind is read by the emit
-- elaboration that follows it. When that happened, the un-mangled ctor `A` was read
-- as a sibling of the mangled survivor, `a.k` was false-rejected, `Display Int` never
-- grounded, and the emitter wrote a null dict word — clean exit 0 and a SIGSEGV at run
-- time, with eval correct throughout, which is why this is pinned as a three-engine
-- fixture and not an eval-side test. Writing `main = println a.k` instead skips the
-- wrap entirely and never reaches the interleaved check; a single-field record gives
-- the sibling check nothing to withhold.

data A = A { p : Int, k : Int }

main =
  let a = A { p = 10, k = 5 }
  a.k
